  "notes": "{解熱剤|げねつざい} is medicine specifically for reducing fever. A practical word to know for pharmacy visits and doctor consultations.\n\nFORMS:\n{解熱|げねつ} (fever reduction) + {剤|ざい} (medicine/agent)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {解熱剤|げねつざい}を{飲|の}む (to take fever reducer)\n- {解熱剤|げねつざい}で{熱|ねつ}を{下|さ}げる (to lower fever with antipyretic)\n- {子供用|こどもよう}の{解熱剤|げねつざい} (children's fever reducer)\n\nCOMMON INGREDIENTS:\n- アセトアミノフェン (acetaminophen)\n- イブプロフェン (ibuprofen)\n\nRELATED MEDICINE WORDS:\n- {鎮痛剤|ちんつうざい}: painkiller\n- {風邪薬|かぜぐすり}: cold medicine\n- {処方薬|しょほうやく}: prescription medicine\n- {市販薬|しはんやく}: over-the-counter medicine",
